From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 14:30:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] UefiPayloadPkg/FmpDeviceSmmLib: Print the manifest entry
 count with %a

The debug message on the region manifest prints "y" or "ies" with %s,
which in DEBUG () is a CHAR16 string: it prints the memory after the
ASCII string until it finds a NUL CHAR16. Use %a.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 UefiPayloadPkg/Library/FmpDeviceSmmLib/FmpDeviceSmmLib.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/FmpDeviceSmmLib/FmpDeviceSmmLib.c b/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/FmpDeviceSmmLib/FmpDeviceSmmLib.c
index 0916b62cba..4fe7bb37f4 100644
--- a/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/FmpDeviceSmmLib/FmpDeviceSmmLib.c
+++ b/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/FmpDeviceSmmLib/FmpDeviceSmmLib.c
@@ -1802,7 +1802,7 @@ FmpDeviceSetImageWithStatus (
   } else {
     DEBUG ((
       DEBUG_INFO,
-      "%a(): found region manifest (%u entr%s), base image size 0x%x\n",
+      "%a(): found region manifest (%u entr%a), base image size 0x%x\n",
       __func__,
       (UINT32)ManifestEntryCount,
       (ManifestEntryCount == 1) ? "y" : "ies",
-- 
